    <statement><p>A function with parameters <m>a</m> and <m>b</m> is given. Describe
the critical points and possible points of
inflection of <m>f</m> in terms of <m>a</m> and <m>b</m>. 
<me>f(x) = (x - a)(x - b)</me></p>
<p>Critical point: <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
<p>Possible point of inflection: <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0002"/></p>
<p>(Separate multiple values with a comma. Enter <alert>NONE</alert> if none exist.)</p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\frac{a+b}{2}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\text{NONE}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><p>Find <m>f'</m> and <m>f''</m>.  Set each
equal to zero and solve to answer the problem.
<m>\displaystyle{  f'(x) = 2x - (a+b) = 0 \;\Rightarrow\; x = \dfrac{a + b}{2}.
}</m><m>f''(x) = 2 = 0</m> has no solution.</p>
</solution>
